\b 29:10-14\b0 
All stand present, from head to water-drawer, to enter \u237?nto the covenant and its oath; God confirms them as a people \u8212? \u225?lso on behalf of the one \u8216?not here today\u8217?.
stepping in \u183? covenant beyond the generation \u183? head to water-drawer
Who enters here, and on whose behalf?


\b 29:15-28\b0 
The root bearing poison is the person who secretly bl\u233?sses himself (29:18). Wrath, exile. Then 29:29: the secret things belong to the LORD; the revealed to \u250?s and our children, \u8216?to do them\u8217?.
hidden \u8596?\u-498? revealed \u183? self-blessing \u183? to do
Why is the secret precisely the root?


\b 30:1-10\b0 
After exile: return (teshuvah), God gathers, and God circumcises the heart (30:6) to love Him.
return \u183? God circumcises \u183? heart freed
What comes first: the freed heart, or the loving?


\b 30:11-14\b0 
The commandment is not too wondrous, not far, not in heaven, not over the sea \u8212? near, in mouth and heart, \u8216?to do it\u8217? (3\u215? la\u8217?asoto; 4QDeut-b/LXX add \u8216?and in your hands\u8217?).
near \u183? in mouth / heart / hands \u183? to do
What does \u8216?near\u8217? mean \u8212? non-committal, or reachable-to-do?


\b 30:15-20\b0 
\u8216?I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing \u8212? ch\u243?ose life.\u8217? Heaven and earth as witnesses.
choose \u183? life / death \u183? witnesses
Why is the choice laid with the human?


\b 31:1-30\b0 
Moses (120) hands over to Joshua (\u8216?be strong and of good courage\u8217?, 31:7); the Torah read aloud every seven years to the wh\u243?le people incl. children and stranger (31:11-12); the song and the Torah bes\u237?de the ark, as witness.
handover \u183? read aloud \u183? witness
Why does passing on belong with the near word?




\par\b\fs28 A2. Connecting hypotheses\b0\fs24\par


\par \b \u8594?\b0  \i Formulate two readings the text could carry, and choose with the test: which explains the most data with the least force?\i0 \par


\par \b Hypothesis 1 (one axis):\b0  the center of gravity is the Source axis alone \u8212? the parashah is grace: God gathers, circumcises the heart (30:6), makes it reachable. The doing then stays secondary.\par


\par \b Hypothesis 2 (relation):\b0  the center of gravity is the rel\u225?tion \u8212? the near word is brought near (Source) precisely to be d\u243?ne and p\u225?ssed on (Will/Coherence). 30:6 is the ground, 30:11-20 + all of Vayelech the mass.\par


\par \b Which explains the most data with the least force?\b0  Hypothesis 2. Hypothesis 1 sees the grace, but makes the rhetorical mass (3\u215? \u8216?to do it\u8217?, \u8216?choose\u8217?, all of Vayelech with the handover) inexplicable. The relation reading grounds the doing \u237?n the given nearness.\par


\par \b What would refute this reading?\b0  If 30:6 (the circumcised heart) stood as climax and 30:11-20 functioned as a subclause, the center of gravity would lie with Source / receiving. The text turns that around \u8212? 30:6 is precondition, not landing place.\par


