\b Will\b0 
29:11 (stepping in) \u183? 30:2 (returning/doing) \u183? 30:11-14 (near doing) \u183? 30:19 (choosing) \u183? 31:7,12 (handing over, hearing-learning-doing)
Bearing. Answer within reach; the word is brought t\u243? you \u8212? no self-sufficiency, yet a real calling.
Where does \u8216?chosen doing\u8217? turn into \u8216?my own strength\u8217? (cf. 8:17)?


\b Coherence\b0 
29:18 (secret self-blessing) \u183? 29:29 (hidden \u8596?\u-498? revealed, to do) \u183? 31:19 (song as witness)
Bearing, second pole. No gap between hidden heart and public deed; arvut \u8212? the people stand surety as one body.
The nekudot on \u8216?us and our children\u8217? \u8212? why a mark on precisely the passed-on responsibility?


\b Source\b0 
30:3-6 (God gathers, circumcises the heart)
Real, but does not carry the weight here \u8212? ground, not climax. The freed heart makes the doing reachable.
Why does 30:6 stand before, and not as landing place?


\b Trajectory\b0 
exile \u8594? return (30:1-5) \u183? Moses \u8594? Joshua (31:7) \u183? generation \u8594? generation (31:12-13)
Rising; feeds the \u8216?passing on\u8217? side, but serves Will, not as a core of its own.
Is \u8216?for ever\u8217? (29:29) a limit, or a promise?




\par \i Reactivity: the reflex puts the weight on receiving / defencelessness (30:6 as climax) \u8212? precisely what the sources contradict. Note it as watch, and do not place it as the motor under the reading.\i0 \par


\par\b\fs28 A4. Movement\b0\fs24\par


\par \b \u8594?\b0  \i Summarize the movement: what does the text unmask, what frame does it put in its place, what response follows \u8212? and capture it in one core sentence.\i0 \par


\par \b What is unmasked?\b0  The word made far away \u8212? in heaven, over the sea, a burden, a yoke imposed (or making yourself a badge); and the person who in secret blesses himself and yet walks his own way (29:18).\par


\par \b What frame does the text put in its place?\b0  The near word: God circumcises the heart (30:6) and brings the word into your mouth, heart and hands (30:11-14) \u8212? reachable to be done, and to be passed on.\par


\par \b What concrete response and formation follow?\b0  Step into the covenant; choose life; read the word aloud and lay it in your child\u8217?s hand (31:11-12); and the self-test \u8212? do I do out of received nearness, or do I grasp and secretly bless myself?\par


\par \b Core sentence: The word is not far \u8212? God brought it near and freed the heart; so step in, choose, do it, and pass it on.\b0 \par


\par \i \b Horizon\b0  (not this week\u8217?s theme, but the ground): beneath all this lies received or grasped. The near-word-to-do is the received-form; the secret self-blessing the grasped-form. In the gospel the near word becomes a Person (John 12): a Mouth that speaks \u8216?not of Itself\u8217?, the Light that came to us.\i0 \par


